Z||000015||Scott2M4||11-19-1999||07:03 AM||||Here's one for you all ...<P>When I purchased my 1987 coupe, the guy threw in a Wolf bra but didn't provide the instruction sheet.  I tried to install it last weekend after a nice bath and wax job (the car, not me!) but I couldn't figure out what all of the hooks and clips connect to.<P>Could someone with a Wolf bra (and their instruction sheet) either try to explain to me how it correctly goes on, or scan the sheet and email it to me?  It would be greatly appreciated.||||reg||5
Z||000016||olympic||11-19-1999||02:30 PM||||I bought a wolf bra from Canadian Tire a few years ago. I'm not sure if they still carry that brand, check it out. Personally, I won't buy another bra for my vehicles. Unless you buy a 3 piece Le Bra(which dont look as good as the one piece Wolf) you have to remove it to open the hood. Also, dirt gets under the Bra and scratches the h*ll out of the paint. You'll also get fade and mildew marks underneath if the car sits in the sun at all.Most bras also flop up and down in the wind at hiway speeds which is very annoying.||||reg||1
