Z||000020||SCCA FIERO||11-20-1999||03:08 PM||||I bought my 88 coupe that once had a bra on it. The bra scuffed the paint and raised the fascia up between it and the hood. I have no idea what brand it was, but it had all the little hooks on it. They were screwed on by the bolts that hold the splashshields on. There is also velcro strips on the fascia where it bolts on the car in front of the hood.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Patrick||11-20-1999||06:28 PM||||<BR>My '87 Coupe had a bra on it when I bought it and I couldn't get it off fast enough. I agree with the earlier statements here about the bra itself causing damage to the paint. A few little paint chips from rocks is nothing compared to the scuff marks, etc. that the bra itself creates.<P>Besides, I could never understand why anyone would want to hide the smooth, streamlined styling of any Fiero under a big chunk of black imitation leather.<P>I know, I know... Different strokes for different folks...||||reg||13
